hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22875","Bahz narrated to us: Hammad informed us: Ishaq, meaning Ibn Abi Talhah, informed us, from Abu al-Mundhir, the freedman of Abu Dharr, from Abu Umayyah al-Makhzumi, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought a thief who confessed, and no goods were found with him. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: I do not think you stole. He said: Yes, two or three times. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Cut him, then bring him to me. He said: So they cut him, then they brought him. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Say: I seek forgiveness from Allah and repent to Him. He said: I seek forgiveness from Allah and repent to Him. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, accept his repentance."
